---
layout: layouts/base.njk
bodyClass: home
---
<main class="landing">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <img class="hero-icon" src="/assets/img/icon.svg" alt="The mido icon: a prompt and the letters md on a dark green tile" width="96" height="96">
      <h1 class="display">mido<span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span></h1>
      <p class="lead">{{ site.tagline }}</p>
      <p class="hero-blurb">{{ site.description }} Built in Rust on ratatui.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/getting-started/">Get started</a>
        <a class="btn" href="{{ site.repo }}">Source on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% include "partials/hero-terminal.njk" %}
  </section>

  <section class="readme glass">
    <div class="prose">
      {{ content | fromFirstSection | safe }}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% if demo.available %}
  <section class="demo">
    <h2 class="title">See it run</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">Recorded with VHS from a tape in the repository and regenerated on every deploy, so it always shows the current release.</p>
    <figure class="demo-frame glass">
      <video autoplay muted loop playsinline controls preload="metadata" aria-label="mido browsing its own documentation in a terminal">
        <source src="/assets/img/demo.webm" type="video/webm">
        <source src="/assets/img/demo.mp4" type="video/mp4">
      </video>
    </figure>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section class="pipeline">
    <h2 class="title">One pipeline, two outputs</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">Every block keeps its source range, so the same model drives the screen, the outline, search, link following and print mode.</p>
    {% include "partials/pipeline.njk" %}
  </section>

  <section class="features">
    <h2 class="title">A reader, not cat with colors</h2>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <a class="feature glass" href="/panels/#files-sidebar">
        <pre class="mini" aria-hidden="true">docs
├ ▾ guide
│  ├ install.md
│  └ keys.md
├ <b>README.md</b>
└ CHANGELOG.md</pre>
        <h3>Browse a folder</h3>
        <p>Open a directory and the Markdown files hang in a tree on the left. It honours .gitignore and starts on the README.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="feature glass" href="/panels/#outline">
        <pre class="mini" aria-hidden="true"><i>╭ Outline ──────╮</i>
<i>│</i> ▾ <b>Install</b>       <i>│</i>
<i>│</i> ▾ Use           <i>│</i>
<i>│</i>   ├ Files       <i>│</i>
<i>│</i>   └ Keys        <i>│</i>
<i>╰───────────────╯</i></pre>
        <h3>Keep the outline in view</h3>
        <p>The headings sit in a card at the top right, fold like a tree and follow where you are reading.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="feature glass" href="/navigation/">
        <pre class="mini" aria-hidden="true">See the <u>keys page</u> for
the full list.

<i>]</i> next   <i>[</i> previous
<i>Enter</i> follow   <i>H</i> back</pre>
        <h3>Follow links, keep history</h3>
        <p>Relative links open in place, anchors jump to their heading, web links open in your browser. Back and forward work like a browser too.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="feature glass" href="/rendering/#mermaid-diagrams">
        <pre class="mini" aria-hidden="true">┌───────┐
│ Start │
└───┬───┘
    ▼
 &lt; Ready? &gt;
  ┌─┘ └─┐
 yes    no
  ▼      ▼
╭────╮ ┌──────┐
│ Go │ │ Wait │
╰────╯ └──────┘</pre>
        <h3>Diagrams in text</h3>
        <p>Mermaid blocks are drawn with box characters. Flowcharts, sequence, class and state diagrams, pie, gantt and more.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta glass">
    <div class="cta-copy">
      <h2 class="title">Built in the open</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">mido is MIT licensed, written in Rust on ratatui, and shaped by the people who read Markdown in a terminal all day. Report a bug, suggest a key, pick up an open issue, or teach it a new element. Every stage of the pipeline has tests to lean on.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ site.repo }}">Contribute on GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn" href="{{ site.repo }}/issues/new">Open an issue</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre class="cta-term" aria-hidden="true"><i>$</i> git clone https://github.com/anistark/mido
<i>$</i> cd mido
<i>$</i> cargo run -- README.md
<i>$</i> <span class="caret"></span></pre>
  </section>
</main>
